00:16:27.269 --> 00:16:31.743
And until next time, remember: It’s ok to be a little crazy.

00:16:33.969 --> 00:16:38.130
What’s the mechanism that converts spacetime curvature into Hawking radiation?

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:40.358
Well, we don't actually know.

00:16:40.358 --> 00:16:45.259
Using general relativity and quantum field theory at the same time can be a bit tricky.

00:16:45.364 --> 00:16:49.354
Hawking managed it using something called a Bogoliubov transformation,

00:16:49.522 --> 00:16:51.670
which is a non-local math tool.

00:16:51.945 --> 00:16:54.875
That means we don’t have a local mechanism for Hawking radiation.

00:16:55.212 --> 00:16:56.212
Yet.

00:16:56.317 --> 00:16:58.002
Anyway, thanks for watching.

